<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarik Sulayman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1571</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarik Sulayman was a chief of Macabebe in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pampanga">Pampanga</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, who led a coalition fleet against the Spanish at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in 1571. Spanish accounts describe him only as the young chief of Macabebe. He was killed when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-de-goiti">Martín de Goiti</a>'s forces defeated the fleet at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bangkusay-channel">Battle of Bangkusay Channel</a> on 3 June 1571, and he is often confused with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-sulayman">Rajah Sulayman</a> of Manila.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarik-sulayman.jpg" alt="Tarik Sulayman" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Judgefloro · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FvfMacabebe9972_30.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
